================================================================================
Specifications implemented or profiled
================================================================================

This work implements, profiles, or extends the specifications below. They are
cited as normative references. No specification text is reproduced in this
repository: every occurrence of specification wording in these files is a
citation URL, verified by ten-word phrase comparison against the published
documents.

  User-Managed Access (UMA) 2.0 Grant for OAuth 2.0 Authorization
  Federated Authorization for UMA 2.0
      Kantara Initiative. https://docs.kantarainitiative.org/uma/

      Copyright (c) 2018 Kantara Initiative and the persons identified as the
      document authors. Both documents are subject to the Kantara IPR Policy,
      Option Patent & Copyright: Reciprocal Royalty Free with Opt-Out to
      Reasonable And Non-discriminatory (RAND), version 2.0.

      Under that policy, Article 4.1(a) of Appendix B grants a royalty-free,
      non-exclusive patent licence to any person or entity, whether or not a
      Kantara Participant, to implement the specification -- to the extent
      needed to be a Fully Compliant Implementation as that policy defines it.
      Article 3 grants a copyright licence to prepare derivative works, and
      that grant runs between Kantara Participants rather than to the public.
      This project relies on neither: it reproduces no specification text, and
      copyright in a specification covers the document, not the protocol it
      describes.

      UMA 2.0 Grant Section 4 contemplates profiles (which restrict UMA's
      options) and extensions (which use its extensibility points), and
      recommends that the creator of one assign it a uniquely identifying URI
      and that an authorization server supporting it advertise that URI in its
      `uma_profiles_supported` metadata. This project is both a profile and a
      set of extensions; the deviations are enumerated in docs/PROTOCOL.md
      under "Extension register". It does not yet mint or advertise a profile
      URI.

